<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore October M1 rises 6.5 pct on year - MAS.</title>
<headline>Singapore October M1 rises 6.5 pct on year - MAS.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Money supply figures.</p>
<p>	   (in billions of Singapore dollars)</p>
<p>				 Oct	Sep	  Oct 95</p>
<p>M-1 (narrow money)	 26.09    26.55	24.50</p>
<p>M-2			   108.70   109.37	98.48</p>
<p>M-3 (broad money)	 135.63   136.37     124.52</p>
<p>Demand deposits	    16.23    16.67	15.03</p>
<p>Currency in active	  9.86     9.88	 9.47</p>
<p>circulation</p>
<p>Note - The Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) said narrow money supply (M1) grew by 6.5 percent year-on-year in October compared with 7.7 percent in September.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
